  "description": "Construction of 1 x 1 bed 1 person 2-storey dwelling with associated external amenity area, parking space, bicycle storage and waste storage",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its siting, design, mass and bulk,&nbsp;would appear at odds with the prevailing character of the host dwelling and terrace row, and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would result in a loss of symmetry to the existing terrace row, disrupt the planned form of the corner piece,&nbsp;and result in&nbsp;a&nbsp;loss of the open aspect and visual amenity of this plot. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D4 and&nbsp;HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1 and DMD4 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development fails to provide clarity that additional demand for parking could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area, or that access of the existing dropped kerb for both properties can be accessed interchangeably and independently from each property.&nbsp; In the absence of this information, officers are unable to determine whether the proposal would result in parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policies T1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
